# Temporary seams, provable in Verus. The constructors take the zeroed
# words on the caller's safety contract until a ghost permission to zeroed
# memory can be passed to them; the accessors read and write through the
# word's permission (`vstd::raw_ptr::ptr_ref`, `ptr_mut_ref`) but stay
# unchecked until the proofs land that the word is in `perms`, that
# `ptr.add(..)` is its permission's pointer, and the writers' frame.
from_raw	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
from_raw_chunked	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
l1	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
l0	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
l1_mut	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
l0_mut	raw pointer (internal)	Verus
